			"Message": "chore(Rest): Expand build script lint allowances for transitional state\n\nAdd broad lint suppressions (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`, `unused_variables`, etc.) to `build.rs` to accommodate the transitional phase of the Rest bundler's strict naming policy adoption.\n\nThese allowances ensure the build script compiles without warnings while upstream dependencies and internal structures are being refactored to full PascalCase compliance, preventing build noise during the migration.",
			"SHA": "8f445120ab754cb7fe562196dbbf1a6eebc6c114"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:21:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				13
			],
			"Message": "style(Rest): Standardize formatting and remove dead code lints\n\nReformat Rust source files in the Rest bundler to comply with strict spacing conventions, adding newlines after block headers and conditional branches. Remove the `#[allow(dead_code)]` attribute from `ParseResult.file_path` as the field is now actively utilized. Clean up test modules by removing redundant `#![cfg(test)]` wrappers which are implicit within `#[cfg(test)]` blocks.\n\nTemporarily expand the `Library.rs` lint allowances to include `dead_code` and unused elements to facilitate the transition from the previous strict naming policy. Rename `tests/lib.rs` to `tests/Library.rs` to maintain PascalCase consistency across the test suite.\n\nThis ensures uniform code style across NLS replacement, OXC/SWC parsing, and worker detection logic while preparing the codebase for full strict linting compliance.",
			"SHA": "0d5c35e2067655a4a94aad27dfaddddbbcf3affc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T03:51:50Z",
